{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":22785,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","packSha":"e09db9448d81c6032511530fa092729cce09664ac6c76d5845551826f2e17038","packTokens":7967,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":67,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":678,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":907,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":6200,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"failures","tokens":37,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":8,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Replace phone/email-based parts ordering with a self-service ordering portal\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Allow customers to quickly find parts using part numbers, product names, categories, and vehicle information\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Show each customer their applicable pricing and current stock availability\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Reduce manual order-entry work for office staff\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Give customers visibility into order status and invoices\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide staff with operational order queues and delivery information\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide management with basic sales and product reporting\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Maintain an auditable history of orders, invoices, customer accounts, and catalogue changes\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-9\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement customer authentication with sign-in, password reset, and account management\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-10\",\n  \"text\": \"Build product catalogue with search, filtering, categories, and vehicle compatibility\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-11\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement customer-specific pricing and price list management\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-12\",\n  \"text\": \"Manage stock availability with ERP CSV imports\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-13\",\n  \"text\": \"Build basket and checkout workflow with delivery date rules\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-14\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement order management with status tracking and staff editing capabilities\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-15\",\n  \"text\": \"Build customer order history, cancellation, and repeat order functionality\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-16\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement invoice creation, viewing, PDF download, and payment tracking\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-17\",\n  \"text\": \"Build administrative tools for product, user, category, and price list management\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Is the Customer Account Manager role part of the first release?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No: first release has Buyer, Office Staff and Administrator only\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Does a Buyer see every order and invoice of their company, or only the ones they placed? The Buyer section says 'their company's orders', but the Account Manager role adds 'orders placed by other users'.\",\n  \"answer\": \"Buyer sees all orders and invoices of their own company\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Which status changes can staff make after confirmation? Can they skip a status, go back a step, or cancel a Confirmed or Picking order?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Forward only, in order (Confirmed → Picking → Out for delivery → Delivered); staff may cancel any order not yet Delivered\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Under 'where permitted', when may staff change the delivery date or address before confirmation?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Always before confirmation, limited to the customer's addresses and dates valid under the cutoff rule\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"What happens to a customer company's users and open orders when the company is set inactive?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Its users cannot sign in or order; existing orders and invoices stay visible to staff\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Buyers see all of their company's orders (answer Q-2). Can a Buyer also cancel or repeat a Received order that a colleague placed, or that staff created for the company?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Any Buyer of the company may cancel or repeat any company order that is eligible\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"With no Customer Account Manager in the first release (answer Q-1), can Buyers add or edit their company's delivery addresses, or do only staff/admins manage them?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Only staff/admins manage addresses; Buyers choose from existing ones\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"For an inactive customer company (answer Q-5), can staff still move its open orders forward, create new orders for it, and have invoices created when its orders are delivered?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Open orders continue as normal and invoices are still created; staff cannot create new orders for the company\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"A sign-in with a matching email and password starts an authenticated session and returns the user's role.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"A sign-in with an unknown email or wrong password is rejected with one identical invalid-credentials error and no session token.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"After five consecutive failed sign-ins, the account is locked for 15 minutes and every sign-in attempt during that time is rejected with a temporary-lock error.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Sign-in attempts and requests made with existing sessions are rejected for a deactivated user or a user of an inactive company, including order submission.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Signing out invalidates the user's session token.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Any endpoint other than sign-in, password reset and invitation acceptance rejects requests lacking a valid session token, returning no record data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"A request outside a user's role capabilities is rejected with a forbidden status; Administrators have all Office Staff capabilities.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"A signed-in Buyer can only see their own company's orders, invoices, prices, delivery addresses and account data; requests for such records of another company return a not-found status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Requesting a password reset sends a single-use reset link valid for a configured period, defaulting to one hour, if the email matches an account, returning the same response either way.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Submitting a new password through an unexpired, unused reset link replaces the password, invalidates the link and clears any sign-in lock on the account.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Submitting a new password through an expired or already-used reset link is rejected and the existing password is kept.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Inviting a user as a Buyer linked to a company, or as Office Staff, creates a pending account and sends an invitation link valid for a configured period, defaulting to seven days.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Inviting a user with the role Administrator creates a pending account and sends an invitation email.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Setting a password through an unexpired invitation link activates the account.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Resending an invitation for a pending account invalidates every previous invitation link for that user and sends a new invitation email.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators can list users with role, company and status, associate a Buyer with a company, and deactivate or reactivate a user without deleting that user's orders or invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators can change a user's role between Buyer and Office Staff.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators can change a user's role to Administrator.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Reactivating a deactivated user whose company is inactive is rejected.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"A catalogue search returns active products whose name, distributor product code, manufacturer part number or brand contains the search term, ignoring letter case.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Listing the catalogue returns active products in the selected category combined with any search term, or all matching active products when no category filter is supplied.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"A vehicle search using any combination of make, model, year, engine, fuel type and variant returns only active products with a compatibility entry matching every supplied value.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"Catalogue listings return only active products, each with image, name, product code, manufacturer, unit of sale, pack size, the Buyer's price and stock status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"Opening an active product returns its image, name, product code, manufacturer, description, unit, pack size, the Buyer's price, stock status and compatible vehicles.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"text\": \"Prices shown to a Buyer and used for basket lines, staff-created orders and repeat orders are taken from the price list currently assigned to the Buyer's company, so a changed assignment applies from then on.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"text\": \"Office Staff can view the unit price a given customer company pays for a product, taken from that company's assigned price list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 27,\n  \"text\": \"A product with no price on a company's assigned price list is shown as price on request and cannot be added to a basket or order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 28,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators can create, rename and deactivate price lists, set, edit and remove at most one price per product on a list, and assign an active price list to a company.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 29,\n  \"text\": \"Changing a price on a price list or a company's price list assignment does not change the unit prices already stored on existing orders and invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 30,\n  \"text\": \"Stock status is derived as out of stock when quantity is zero or never imported, low stock up to a configured threshold, and in stock above that threshold.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 31,\n  \"text\": \"A scheduled stock import that finds a valid new file replaces stored quantities and recalculates stock status for each listed known product, and logs a successful import with row counts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 32,\n  \"text\": \"A valid import file containing unknown product identifiers skips those rows, applies the other rows, and lists the unknown identifiers in the import log.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 33,\n  \"text\": \"A missing, unreadable, empty or invalid import file, or no new file since the last run, leaves every stock quantity unchanged and logs a failed import with the reason.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 34,\n  \"text\": \"Listing stock imports returns each import's time, status, rows-applied count, skipped identifiers and failure reason.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 35,\n  \"text\": \"No create, update or delete request is ever sent to the ERP system.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 36,\n  \"text\": \"Opening a product as a staff user returns its imported stock quantity, stock status, the time of the last successful import and its price on each price list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 37,\n  \"text\": \"A basket or order change that would set a quantity above the available stock, or involves an out-of-stock product, is rejected with an error stating the available quantity.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 38,\n  \"text\": \"While a Buyer's session is active, the basket persists across navigation, allows adding products, changing line quantity with a minimum of one, and removing lines, shows each line's price, quantity and total and the overall subtotal, and is discarded when the session ends.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 39,\n  \"text\": \"The earliest delivery date is calculated, in the configured timezone, as the next working day for orders before the configured cutoff, defaulting to 14:00, or the following working day for orders at or after the cutoff, skipping configured non-working dates.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 40,\n  \"text\": \"Only working days from the earliest delivery date up to a configured maximum number of days ahead are offered and accepted as delivery dates, re-checked at submission, with any other date rejected with an error naming the delivery date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 41,\n  \"text\": \"A basket, order submission or order edit with a delivery address not belonging to the order's company is rejected with an error naming the delivery address.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 42,\n  \"text\": \"Submitting an order re-checks every line's availability, stock limit and current price, and rejects the submission while listing the affected lines with current price and available quantity if any line is unavailable, over stock or re-priced.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 43,\n  \"text\": \"Proceeding to checkout displays a final review page with the lines, quantities, unit prices, line totals, subtotal, delivery address, delivery date and note before the submit action.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 44,\n  \"text\": \"Submitting a valid order creates it with the next sequential prefixed order number, lines at order-time unit prices, a copy of the delivery address, the delivery date, an optional note, status Received and a first timeline entry, and then empties the basket.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 45,\n  \"text\": \"An order submitted by a deactivated user, a user of an inactive company, or staff creating an order for an inactive company, is rejected and no order is created.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 46,\n  \"text\": \"Every order status change adds a timeline entry recording the new status, the date and time, and the user who made the change or the system.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 47,\n  \"text\": \"Order emails are sent to the Buyer who placed the order, or to the customer company's contact email when staff created the order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 48,\n  \"text\": \"A Buyer listing orders sees every order of their company, including those placed by colleagues or created by staff, with order number, dates, delivery address, total and status, filterable by status and date range.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 49,\n  \"text\": \"Opening an order, as the company's Buyer or as staff, returns its number, dates, customer, delivery address, status, status timeline, lines, totals, note and staff amendments.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 50,\n  \"text\": \"A Buyer cancelling their own company's order while it is in Received status sets it to Cancelled and adds a timeline entry with the Buyer and time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 51,\n  \"text\": \"A Buyer trying to cancel an order that is not in Received status is rejected with an error telling them to contact the distributor office.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 52,\n  \"text\": \"Repeating an order adds each still-orderable line to the basket at the current price and original quantity, capped at available stock and flagged when reduced, flags retired, out-of-stock or unpriced lines as unavailable, and creates no order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 53,\n  \"text\": \"Staff listing orders see orders of all customers with order number, customer, dates, total and status, filterable by customer, date range and status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 54,\n  \"text\": \"Staff searching customers by partial name or account number, or opening a customer company, see matching companies, or for the opened company its details, delivery addresses, assigned price list, users, status, orders and invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 55,\n  \"text\": \"Staff editing an order can change line quantities, remove lines, change the note, change the delivery address to another address of the same company, and change the delivery date to a currently selectable one, only while the order is in Received status, with edits to orders in any other status rejected.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 56,\n  \"text\": \"A staff quantity change or line removal on a Received order is recorded as an amendment with old and new quantity, staff user and time, and triggers an email to the order recipient listing the changed lines.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 57,\n  \"text\": \"Staff confirming a Received order whose lines are all active and within available stock and whose delivery address still exists sets it to Confirmed with a timeline entry, otherwise rejecting confirmation and listing the failing lines.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 58,\n  \"text\": \"An order becoming Confirmed triggers a confirmation email to the order recipient containing the order number, lines, totals, delivery address, delivery date and any quantity changes made before confirmation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 59,\n  \"text\": \"Staff can advance an order's status only to the next status in the defined sequence or to cancellation, adding a timeline entry, with any other change rejected and the status left unchanged.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 60,\n  \"text\": \"An order's status becoming Out for delivery triggers an email to the order recipient identifying the order and stating it is out for delivery.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 61,\n  \"text\": \"Staff cancelling or rejecting an order that is neither Delivered nor Cancelled must supply a reason, which sets the status to Cancelled, records the reason, staff user and time, and triggers an email to the recipient containing the reason.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 62,\n  \"text\": \"Staff can submit an order on behalf of an active customer company, under the same price, stock, address and delivery-date rules as a Buyer order, created in Received status and marked as created by that staff user.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 63,\n  \"text\": \"While a customer company is inactive, its existing orders and invoices remain visible to staff, who can still progress, cancel and invoice its open orders.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 64,\n  \"text\": \"Exporting the delivery list for a date, defaulting to today, returns a CSV file with one row per non-Cancelled order due that date, containing order number, customer, delivery address, contact details, delivery date, line summary, note and status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 65,\n  \"text\": \"Opening the staff dashboard returns counts of orders in Received, Picking and Out for delivery status, non-Cancelled orders due for delivery today, and Unpaid and Overdue invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 66,\n  \"text\": \"The staff dashboard also returns the count of orders in Confirmed status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 67,\n  \"text\": \"The staff dashboard also returns the count of failed stock imports since the last successful import.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 68,\n  \"text\": \"When the most recent stock import has failed, the staff dashboard shows that result with its failure time and reason.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 69,\n  \"text\": \"An order's status becoming Delivered creates one invoice with the next sequential prefixed invoice number, customer, the company's billing address, the order number, invoice date, the order lines at order-time prices, net total, the configured tax rate and amount, gross total and status Unpaid.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 70,\n  \"text\": \"An unpaid invoice's payment status is reported as Overdue once more than a configured number of days have passed since its invoice date, as Unpaid before that, and as Paid once payment is recorded.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 71,\n  \"text\": \"Listing invoices returns invoice number, order number, invoice date, gross total and payment status for every invoice of the Buyer's own company, or of all companies for staff.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 72,\n  \"text\": \"Office Staff can list and view all invoices, filterable by customer and payment status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 73,\n  \"text\": \"Downloading an invoice, as the company's Buyer or as staff, returns a PDF file containing the invoice number, invoice date, customer, billing address, order number, lines, totals, payment status, and the distributor's logo and company details.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 74,\n  \"text\": \"Marking an Unpaid or Overdue invoice as paid with a payment date no later than today sets its status to Paid and records the payment date and the staff user.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 75,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators can add, edit and retire products with defined identifying and descriptive fields, keeping retired products out of the catalogue but visible on existing orders and invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 76,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators can create, rename and retire single-level categories and assign each product to one category, hiding retired categories from the Buyer category filter.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 77,\n  \"text\": \"Uploading a product image stores it as the product's image in cloud storage, replacing any previous image, only if it is a JPEG, PNG or WebP file of at most 10 megabytes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 78,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators can add and remove any number of vehicle compatibility entries, each with make, model, model year range, engine, fuel type and variant, on a product.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 79,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators can create and edit customer companies with name, unique account number, primary contact, contact email, contact phone, billing address, assigned price list and active or inactive status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 80,\n  \"text\": \"Adding, editing and removing a customer company's delivery addresses is restricted to staff and administrators, while every delivery address of a Buyer's own company is returned to that Buyer.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 81,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators can view and change the order cutoff time, system timezone, non-working dates, maximum delivery days ahead, low-stock threshold, overdue days, tax rate, order and invoice number prefixes, reset and invitation link validity periods, and the company details and logo used on invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 82,\n  \"text\": \"Every order, invoice, customer company, user, product, category and price list record stores who created it and when and who last changed it and when, and these fields are returned to administrators.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 83,\n  \"text\": \"Office Staff and Administrators can request a sales report for a date range, optionally filtered by customer, showing order count and net total per customer and quantity sold and net total per product from non-Cancelled orders, both as an on-screen list and as a CSV file.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<failures>\nYour previous attempt was rejected for these reasons. Fix them:\n- [runner-over-budget] over-budget\n</failures>\n\nMap the sentences."}